1. Repository lene ke baad
Agar Local VS Code use karna ho
git clone <REPOSITORY_URL>
cd <REPOSITORY_NAME>
code .

Example:

git clone https://github.com/username/project.git
cd project
code .

code . VS Code mein current folder open karta hai.

2. Python version check
python --version

Windows mein ye bhi useful:

py --version

Available Python versions:

py -0p
3. Virtual Environment banana ⭐

Exam mein Python project ho to ye yaad rakho:

Windows
python -m venv .venv

ya:

py -3.13 -m venv .venv
Activate

PowerShell:

.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1

CMD:

.venv\Scripts\activate

Successful hone par:

(.venv) PS C:\...

dikhega.

Deactivate
deactivate
4. Dependencies install karna ⭐⭐⭐

Sabse pehle project mein check:

requirements.txt

hai ya nahi.

Agar hai:

pip install -r requirements.txt

Ye bahut important command hai.

Installed packages check:
pip list
Pip update:
python -m pip install --upgrade pip

Lekin exam mein unnecessarily pip update mat karna. README mein jo diya ho, wahi follow karo.

5. Agar requirements.txt nahi hai

Agar README mein specific packages diye hain:

pip install pytest

Example:

pip install flask
pip install pandas
pip install numpy

Multiple:

pip install pytest coverage pytest-cov
6. Project ko run karna ⭐⭐⭐

Ye project-dependent hai. README dekho.

Common commands:

Python file
python app.py

or

python main.py
Module
python -m <module>
Streamlit
streamlit run app.py
FastAPI/Uvicorn
uvicorn main:app --reload

Exam mein random command nahi lagani. README/project files mein jo entry point ho, uske according run karna.

7. Testing ⭐⭐⭐

Agar project mein pytest hai:

pytest

Detailed:

pytest --verbose

Coverage:

pytest --cov=src --verbose

Coverage report:

coverage report

Hamare GitHub Skills practice mein exactly:

pytest --cov=src --verbose

use hua tha.

8. Git status ⭐⭐⭐

Change karne ke baad sabse pehle:

git status

Ye batayega kaunsi files modified/untracked hain.

Example:

modified: app.py
9. Git add ⭐⭐⭐

Specific file:

git add app.py

All changes:

git add .

Exam ke liye:

git add .

yaad rakh sakta hai.

10. Git commit ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐
git commit -m "Implement required changes"

Examples:

git commit -m "Fix login functionality"
git commit -m "Add unit tests"

Commit message meaningful hona chahiye.

11. Git push ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐

Normally:

git push

Agar first push/current branch specify karni ho:

git push origin main
12. Agar git push reject ho jaye ⭐⭐⭐

Kabhi remote repository mein changes already hote hain.

Error kuch aisa:

rejected
non-fast-forward

Tab:

git pull --rebase origin main

phir:

git push

Hamare practice mein exactly ye situation aayi thi.

So remember:

git push
   ↓
rejected?
   ↓
git pull --rebase origin main
   ↓
git push
13. Git history check
git log --oneline

Isse commits dikhenge.

Latest commit:

git log -1
14. Git branch check
git branch

Current branch:

git branch --show-current

Usually exam repo mein:

main
15. Remote repository check
git remote -v

Output mein GitHub repository ka URL dikhega.

16. GitHub Actions

Iske liye generally terminal command nahi hoti.

GitHub website:

Repository
   ↓
Actions
   ↓
Workflow
   ↓
Latest Run
   ↓
Success ✅ / Failure ❌

Agar workflow push event par configured hai:

git commit
    ↓
git push
    ↓
GitHub Actions automatically
    ↓
Tests
    ↓
Result
17. GitHub Actions workflow manually run karna

Agar workflow mein:

workflow_dispatch:

configured hai, tab GitHub Actions page par Run workflow button aa sakta hai.
